{
  "tema": 6464,
  "slug": "ninguno-pronombre",
  "titulo": "Ninguno, ninguna as pronouns (none, not one)",
  "subtitulo": "No tengo ninguno. Ninguna me queda.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "Without a noun, ninguno / ninguna means none, not one, not any (from a known group). It agrees with the noun it replaces, is almost always singular, and is never shortened to ningún. After the verb you need no before it; before the verb you don't.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Use **ninguno, ninguna** without a noun to say _none, not one_ of something already mentioned."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It agrees with the noun it replaces and is **almost always singular**: **Ninguno de mis primos vino.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Ningunos, ningunas** exist only for nouns that are always plural (**lentes, pantalones**): **No traje ningunos.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "As a pronoun it's always **ninguno**, never **ningún**. **Ningún** only goes right before a masculine noun."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Position",
            "Pattern",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "After the verb",
              "no + verb + ninguno",
              "No me gusta ninguna."
            ],
            [
              "Before the verb",
              "ninguno + verb",
              "Ninguna me gusta."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Ninguno de** + group: **ninguno de nosotros**. For _nobody_ in general, use **nadie**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿Tienes cerillos? —No, no tengo ==ninguno==.",
              "en": "Do you have matches? —No, I don't have any."
            },
            {
              "es": "Probé tres tablas y ==ninguna== me gustó.",
              "en": "I tried three boards and I didn't like any of them."
            },
            {
              "es": "De mis primos, ==ninguno== habla inglés.",
              "en": "None of my cousins speaks English."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué película quieres ver? —==Ninguna==; estoy muy cansado.",
              "en": "Which movie do you want to watch? —None; I'm really tired."
            },
            {
              "es": "Busqué semillas de chile, pero no encontré ==ninguna==.",
              "en": "I looked for chili seeds, but I didn't find a single one."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Ninguno de== nosotros sabía la respuesta.",
              "en": "None of us knew the answer."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Tienes lentes de sol? —No traje ==ningunos==.",
              "en": "Do you have sunglasses? —I didn't bring any."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Tengo ninguno."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "No tengo ninguno."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "After the verb, add **no**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "No ninguno funciona."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Ninguno funciona."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Before the verb, no **no**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "¿Hay toallas? —No hay ningún."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "¿Hay toallas? —No hay ninguna."
                }
